  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final text sets a 7% permanent S2 failure cap with no mandatory sales stop, and a 24-month new-unit shut-off deadline in S3, both looser than the answer-key safe levels. S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective alternative, with regulator-defined recall scope, which costs Halcyon's Ember 8 directly. S1 is the strongest section, with 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents."
 },
